    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Benjamin \"Ben\" McAdams is a community organizer who has served as a Democratic precinct committeeman in York and Bloomingdale townships. He majored in finance and economics at Elmhurst University and focused on public interest law at DePaul University. He previously worked for the National Immigrant Justice Center and Citizen Advocacy Center. He supports public investments to transition Illinois to a 100% green energy economy. In a candidate questionnaire, he said he would invest in public healthcare to offset federal Medicaid cuts and expired Affordable Care Act subsidies. He proposes regulations to keep AI data centers away from residential areas and ensure they are built sustainably. He also pledges to curtail ICE raids.",
